  "body": "It bothers me that we don't have a formalism we can use whenever we defer to something that might be implementation-dependent. See https://github.com/tc39/proposal-intl-segmenter/issues/20, https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/issues/46, and https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3275 for recent instances I came across.\r\n\r\nNote that in some of these cases it's still quite restricted what the implementation can actually do or return.\r\n\r\nThe second of those is interesting as it's actually tightly coupled to what `navigator.platform;` returns. It would be nice to enforce such coupling in a normative matter (and not just tests).\r\n\r\nI'm also not sure if we want to use the word \"platform\" for this as it gets confusing with \"web platform\" and such.\r\n\r\nI think Infra could help by describing this phenomenon and given it a common term we can use everywhere. I'm not entirely sure how to address the tight coupling though.\r\n\r\ncc @mkruisselbrink @inexorabletash @littledan @Ms2ger",
